Oxygen delivery is a measure of the total oxygen available to the tissues, which is influenced by factors such as lung function, lung capacity, and lung efficiency. It is calculated by multiplying oxygen diffusion rate with oxygen diffusion capacity. Oxygen diffusion rate is the rate at which oxygen diffuses from the alveoli into the alveoli. Oxygen diffusion capacity is the rate at which oxygen diffuses from the alveoli into the alveoli.

