To find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Ph-Fol wash, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the concentration to mg/mL:**  
   The concentration is given as 0.044% (w/v), which means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of solution.  
   \[
   \text{Concentration (mg/mL)} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 0.44 \text{ mg/mL}
   \]

2. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:**  
   Multiply the concentration (mg/mL) by the volume (10 mL) to find the mass of sodium fluoride in the 10 mL dose.  
   \[
   \text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = 0.44 \text{ mg/mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
   \]

   The mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose is \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\).
