ΔHhydration(products) = (-392 kJ/mol) + 2 * (-246 kJ/mol)
ΔHhydration(products) = -392 kJ/mol - 492 kJ/mol
ΔHhydration(products) = -884 kJ/mol

Now, we can calculate the standard enthalpy change for the reaction:

ΔH = ΔHhydration(reactants) - ΔHhydration(products)
ΔH = (-1102 kJ/mol) - (-884 kJ/mol)
ΔH = -1102 kJ/mol + 884 kJ/mol
ΔH = -218 kJ/mol

