\]
The complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` is a salt with a positive ion `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]^(2+)` and a negative ion `Cl^{2-}`. When it dissolves in water, it dissociates into its ions:
\[
[\text{Pt(NH}_3\text{)}_4\text{Cl}_2]^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^- \rightarrow [\text{Pt(NH}_3\text{)}_4\text{Cl}_2]^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^-
\]
Thus, the complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates into one `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]^(2+)` ion and two `Cl^-` ions. Therefore, the number of chloride ions produced is 2.

