   - The failure rate is the negative of the failure rate: \( \lambda_S = -\frac{d}{dt} \ln R_S(t) \).  
   - The failure rate of a single component is \( \lambda_i = -\frac{d}{dt} \log R_i(t) \).  
   - The failure rate of the system is: \( \lambda_S = \sum_{i=1}^n \lambda_i = -\sum_{i=1}^n \frac{d}{dt} \log R_i(t) \).  
   - The failure rate of the system is: \( \lambda_S = -\frac{d}{dt} \log R_S(t) \).  
   - Thus, \( \log R_S(t) = \int \sum_{i=1}^n \lambda_i \, dt = \sum_{i=1}^n \int \lambda_i \, dt = \sum_{i=1}^n \lambda_i t + \beta \).  
