   a. **Alcohols**: The hydroxyl group (OH) is attached to a carbon atom in a different position in the carbon skeleton. There are four constitutional isomers in this class:
   - **1-butanol (n-butanol)**: CH3-CH2-CH2-CH2-OH (primary alcohol)
   - **2-butanol (isobutanol)**: CH3-CH(OH)-CH2-CH3 (secondary alcohol)
   - **2-methylpropanol (tert-butanol)**: CH3-C(OH)-CH2-CH3 (tertiary alcohol)
   - **2-methylpropanol (tert-butanol)**: CH3-C(OH)-CH2-CH3 (termary alcohol)

