   - Aldehydes are highly reactive to reducing agents like sodium borohydride (NaBH₄) and lithium aluminum hydride (LiAlH₄).
   - Esters are less reactive to reducing agents like NaBH₄. LiAlH₄ can reduce esters to alcohols, but it is a stronger reagent and may also react with the chloromethyl group.
