<start_of_turn>model
","a) **Series System:**  
   - In a series system, the system fails if only one component fails because the system cannot function without all components working.  
   - If the failure rates of the components are \( \lambda_1, \lambda_2, \ldots, \lambda_n \), the failure rates of the system are the sum of the failure rates of the components: \( \lambda_S = \sum_{i=1}^n \lambda_i \).  
