2. **Determine the moles of oxygen:**
   \[
   \text{Moles of oxygen} = \frac{57.5 \text{ g}}{32 \text{ g/mol}} = 1.80 \text{ moles}
   \]

3. **Calculate the moles of sulfur required:**
   \[
   \text{Moles of sulfur} = \frac{1.80 \text{ moles}}{2} = 0.90 \text{ moles}
   \]

4. **Convert moles of sulfur to mass:**
   \[
   \text{Weight of sulfur} = 0.90 \text{ moles} \times 32 \text{ g/mol} = 28.8 \text{ g}
   \]

