   \[
   \text{Weight of SO₂} = 0.90 \text{ moles} \times 64 \text{ g/mol} = 57.6 \text{ g}
   \]

6. **Calculate the weight of the remaining gas:**
   \[
   \text{Weight of remaining gas} = 250 \text{ g} - 57.5 \text{ g} + 57.6 \text{ g} = 250.1 \text{ g}
   \]

**Final Answers:**
- The amount of sulphur (S) that should be burnt in air to remove oxygen as SO₂ is \(\boxed{28.8 \text{ g}}\).
- The weight of the residual gases in air is \(\boxed{250.1 \text{ g}}\).
