The equation of the line tangent to the graph of a differentiable function \( f \) at the point \( (a, f(a)) \) is given by the equation of a tangent line at a point on a curve. The slope of the tangent line at \( x = a \) is the derivative of \( f \) evaluated at \( a \), denoted as \( f'(a) \). The point on the line is \( (a, f(a)) \). Using the point-slope form of a line, the equation is:

