where \( \ddot{x} \) is the acceleration, \( \dot{x} \) is the velocity, \( y \) is the displacement, \( \omega \) is the angular frequency, and \( \mu \) is the damping constant.  

This equation is a second-order ordinary differential equation. The solution depends on the value of \( \mu \):  
