where \( \beta \) is the absorption coefficient and \( l \) is the length of the medium.

The reflectivity \( R \) is given by the equation:
\[
R = \frac{B \omega}{A + B \omega}
\]
where \( \omega = \omega_0 - \omega \), and \( \omega_0 \) is the frequency of the incident light and \( \omega \) is the frequency of the emitted light.

