\]
Substituting the given values:
\[
A_{fw} = \frac{100}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{100}{0.9} \approx 111.11 \text{ V}
\]
The amplifier's gain decreases by 6 dB due to aging. The new forward gain \( A'_v \) is:
\[
A'_v = \frac{A_v}{10} = \frac{100}{10} = 10
\]
The new closed-loop voltage gain \( A'_{vf} \) is:
\[
A_{vff} = \frac{A'_v}{1 - m_y} = \frac{10}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{10}{0.9} \approx 11.11 \text{ V}
\]
The percentage change in the closed-loop gain is:
\[
\text{Percentage change} = \left( \frac{A_{vff} - A_{fw}}{A_{fw}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{11.11 - 111.11}{111.11} \right) \times 100 \approx \left( \frac{-100}{111.11} \right) \times 100 \approx -89.9\%
\]
Thus, the percentage change in the closed-loop gain is approximately \(\boxed{-89.9\%}\).
