","The maximum percentage change in the wavelength of a 2.00 Å photon scattered by an electron is given by the Compton angle \( \theta = 180^\circ \). The Compton formula for the shift in wavelength is:  
\[
\Delta \lambda = \lambda_0 \left( \frac{1 - \cos \theta}{2} \right)
\]  
For maximum shift (\( \theta = 180^\circ \)), \( \cos 180^\circ = -1 \), so:  
\[
\Delta \lambda = \lambda_0 \left( \frac{1 - (-1)}{2} \right) = \lambda_0 \left( \frac{2}{2} \right) = \lambda_0
\]  
