\[
P = \frac{nR T}{V}
\]  
Substituting this into the work formula:  
\[
W = \int_{V_i}^{V_f} \frac{nR T}{V} \, dV
\]  
Since \( n \) and \( T \) are constant (isothermal process), we can pull them out from the integral:  
\[
W = nRT \int_{V_i}^{V_f} \frac{1}{V} \, dV
\]  
The integral of \( \frac{1}{V} \) is \( \ln V \):  
\[
W = nRT \ln V \bigg|_{V_i}^{V_f} = nRT \ln \left( \frac{V_f}{V_i} \right)
\]  
The volume is expanded by a factor of \( n \), so \( V_f = n V_i \). Substituting this:  
\[
W = nRT \ln \left( \frac{n V_i}{V_i} \right) = nRT \ln n
\]  
Thus, the work done is:  
\[
\boxed{W = nRT \ln n}
\]
